{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"files\":[{\"content\":\"#define _POSIX_C_SOURCE 200112L\\n#include <stdint.h>\\n#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n\\n#define CONV_THRESHOLD 1.0e-5f\\n\\nstatic double *grid;\\nstatic double *new_grid;\\nstatic size_t row_stride;\\nstatic int size;\\nstatic int iter_max_num;\\n\\nstatic int allocate_memory(void) {\\n    size_t n = (size_t)size;\\n    if (n > SIZE_MAX - 7u)\\n        return 0;\\n\\n    row_stride = (n + 7u) & ~(size_t)7u;\\n    if (row_stride > SIZE_MAX / n / sizeof(double))\\n        return 0;\\n\\n    size_t bytes = row_stride * n * sizeof(double);\\n    void *allocation = NULL;\\n    if (posix_memalign(&allocation, 64, bytes) != 0)\\n        return 0;\\n    grid = (double *)allocation;\\n\\n    allocation = NULL;\\n    if (posix_memalign(&allocation, 64, bytes) != 0) {\\n        free(grid);\\n        grid = NULL;\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n    new_grid = (double *)allocation;\\n    return 1;\\n}\\n\\nstatic void initialize_grid(void) {\\n    int center = size / 2;\\n    int linf = center - (size / 10);\\n    int lsup = center + (size / 10);\\n\\n    for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {\\n        size_t row = (size_t)i * row_stride;\\n        for (int j = 0; j < size; j++) {\\n            double value = (i >= linf && i <= lsup &&\\n                            j >= linf && j <= lsup) ? 100.0 : 0.0;\\n            grid[row + (size_t)j] = value;\\n            new_grid[row + (size_t)j] = value;\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nstatic void save_grid(void) {\\n    for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {\\n        size_t row = (size_t)i * row_stride;\\n        for (int j = 0; j < size; j++)\\n            fprintf(stdout, \\\"%lf \\\", grid[row + (size_t)j]);\\n        fprintf(stdout, \\\"\\\\n\\\");\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nint main(void) {\\n    if (fscanf(stdin, \\\"%d\\\", &size) != 1 ||\\n        fscanf(stdin, \\\"%d\\\", &iter_max_num) != 1)\\n        return 0;\\n\\n    if (size <= 0)\\n        return 0;\\n    if (!allocate_memory())\\n        return 1;\\n    initialize_grid();\\n\\n    int hasError = 0;\\n    int keep_going = 1;\\n\\n    /* Keep one team for all timesteps. The completed reduction and buffer\\n       swap precede a uniform convergence decision for the next iteration. */\\n    #pragma omp parallel\\n    {\\n        for (int iter = 0; iter < iter_max_num && keep_going; iter++) {\\n            #pragma omp for schedule(static) reduction(|:hasError)\\n            for (int i = 1; i < size - 1; i++) {\\n                int row_error = 0;\\n                size_t row = (size_t)i * row_stride;\\n                const double * restrict current = grid + row;\\n                const double * restrict above = current - row_stride;\\n                const double * restrict below = current + row_stride;\\n                double * restrict next = new_grid + row;\\n\\n                #pragma omp simd reduction(|:row_error)\\n                for (int j = 1; j < size - 1; j++) {\\n                    next[j] = 0.25 * (current[j + 1] + current[j - 1] +\\n                                      above[j] + below[j]);\\n                    double delta = next[j] - current[j];\\n                    if (delta > CONV_THRESHOLD || delta < -CONV_THRESHOLD)\\n                        row_error |= 1;\\n                }\\n                hasError |= row_error;\\n            }\\n\\n            #pragma omp single\\n            {\\n                double *temporary = grid;\\n                grid = new_grid;\\n                new_grid = temporary;\\n                keep_going = hasError;\\n                hasError = 0;\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    save_grid();\\n    free(grid);\\n    free(new_grid);\\n    return 0;\\n}\\n\",\"path\":\"src/laplace_seq.c\"}],\"hypothesis\":\"Combining the measured aligned, padded buffers and row-local SIMD/reduction stencil with a persistent OpenMP team may reduce repeated team startup and per-timestep synchronization overhead while preserving Jacobi updates and convergence behavior.\",\"notes\":\"This is a speculative integrated candidate; correctness and performance remain for the controller to evaluate.\",\"research\":{\"queries\":[],\"urls\":[]},\"sources_kept\":[\"f9487d1626524047\",\"c22ea45b2c1a48d2\",\"14fee20610e2489e\"],\"transformations\":[\"Retain 64-byte-aligned contiguous buffers with a row stride padded to a multiple of eight doubles; initialize both buffers identically and swap only after each completed stencil update.\",\"Use row-local restrict pointers, static row worksharing, SIMD reduction within each row, and integer-OR convergence reduction.\",\"Keep a persistent parallel team; after each completed timestep, combine the convergence result and swap buffers in one single region before all threads make the same loop-continuation decision.\"]}"}}
